course: dictionary
lesson: 9319
title: Spend: pay out money or use up time
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: The word spend has two main meanings. To spend money is to pay it out for something you buy. To spend time is to use time doing something or being somewhere. «Spend a day at the zoo» means you are at the zoo for the whole day.
explain: Look at the words around spend to find its meaning. If money or a price comes near it, spend means pay out. «Some children have spent hundreds» means they paid out a lot of money. If a time, a day or a place comes near it, spend means use time.
explain: Spend is a verb, so its form changes: spend, spends, spent, spending. You spend today and you spent yesterday. «He spent days in hospital» uses spent because it is about the past.
fact: Spend means to pay out money. «Some children have spent hundreds» means they paid out a lot of money.
fact: To spend time means to use time doing something or being somewhere: «spend a day at the zoo».
fact: «Spent» is the past form: «it helped prove storks spend winter in Africa» shows the present form, and «he spent days in hospital» shows the past.
fact: Common phrases with spend include spend on, spend time, spend the night and spend wisely, which means using money carefully.
fact: «Most grown-ups spend about a third of their weekdays at work» tells you that spend here means use up time.
exercise: Mia had 10 coins and spent 4 of them. How many coins are left? | *6 | 4 | 14 | 5
exercise: «Most grown-ups spend about a third of their weekdays at work.» What does spend mean here? | To hide something | To pay out money | *To use up time | To break something
exercise: «A teenager spent days in hospital.» What does spent mean here? | *Used up time being in hospital | Paid out money for a room | Lost the days | Fell asleep for days
test: «It helped prove storks spend winter in Africa.» Where do the storks spend winter? | *In Africa | In the sea | In Germany | In the mud
test: Which word means the same as spend in «spend wisely»? | Count again | Give away quickly | Lose on purpose | *Use carefully
exam: Leo had 20 cards, spent 7 on Monday and 5 on Tuesday. How many cards are left? | *8 | 27 | 13 | 12
